---
import ArticleLayout from "../../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import InShort from '../../../components/article/InShort.astro';
import ZenTip from '../../../components/article/ZenTip.astro';
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Free 7-Day Stress & Sleep Journal"
  description="A free printable journal for sleep, stress, activity and optional wearable observations. No signup, hormone estimate or health-data upload."
  updated="2026-11-12"
  published="2026-09-09"
>
<InShort points={[
  'Write down sleep, mood and routines for <strong>seven days</strong>.',
  'Use it <strong>with or without</strong> a wearable. No signup.',
  'It <strong>doesn\'t measure cortisol</strong> or prove what caused a change.',
]} />

<h2>Notice patterns over a week</h2>
<p><strong>This journal helps you note how you feel next to your sleep and daily routines.</strong></p>
<p>You can use it with or without a wearable.</p>
<p>It does not measure cortisol or show that one habit caused a change.</p>
<p><a href="/resources/stress-sleep-journal.csv" download>Download the blank CSV</a> or <button id="print-journal" class="underline">print this journal</button>.</p>
<p>What you type stays on this page only, so copy or print it before you leave. It isn't saved or sent to analytics.</p>

<h2>Choose one thing to notice</h2>
<p><strong>Write one simple question</strong>, like "How do I feel after different bedtimes?"</p>
<p>Keep your notes to what happened. Try not to change several routines at once and then treat the result as proof something worked.</p>

<ZenTip image="/app-ui/zen_new_tour_sleep.webp">
  Fill in each day <strong>soon after you wake up</strong>, while last night is still fresh.
</ZenTip>

<div class="journal-pages">
  {Array.from({ length: 7 }, (_, i) => (
    <fieldset class="journal-day border rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
      <legend class="font-bold px-2">Day {i + 1}</legend>
      <label class="block my-3">Date and sleep timing<input class="block w-full border rounded p-2" type="text" placeholder="Date · bedtime · wake time · estimated sleep" /></label>
      <label class="block my-3">How I feel<textarea class="block w-full border rounded p-2" rows="2" placeholder="Energy, mood and anything I noticed" /></label>
      <label class="block my-3">Routine and context<textarea class="block w-full border rounded p-2" rows="2" placeholder="Activity, caffeine timing, unusual events or illness" /></label>
      <label class="block my-3">Optional wearable observation<input class="block w-full border rounded p-2" type="text" placeholder="Device · metric · time recorded · missing data" /></label>
    </fieldset>
  ))}
</div>

<h2>Example entry (made up)</h2>
<p>"Tuesday: bed 11:30 p.m., up 7:00 a.m.; felt tired on waking. Busy afternoon, coffee at 3 p.m., short evening walk. Watch HRV record from 6:40 a.m. available; no conclusion about cortisol."</p>
<p>These values are just an example. They're not a target to aim for or a real customer's result.</p>

<a href="/start/" data-start-cta class="not-prose my-8 flex items-center gap-4 rounded-2xl bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-5 text-white no-underline shadow-sm transition hover:brightness-110">
  <img src="/apple-touch-icon.png" alt="" width="48" height="48" class="h-12 w-12 shrink-0 rounded-[13px]" />
  <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 leading-snug">
    <span class="block font-extrabold">Get your personal stress plan</span>
    <span class="block text-sm text-white/75">A one-minute check-in with Zen, then your plan in Cortisol+</span>
  </span>
  <span class="shrink-0 rounded-full bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-extrabold text-[color:var(--color-ink)]">Start ›</span>
</a>

<h2>At the end of seven days</h2>
<p><strong>Look back and ask yourself:</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>Which routines stayed the same? Which days were unusual?</li>
  <li>Did the wearable data match how you felt? Write down where it didn't, too.</li>
  <li>What's one question to explore next week, or to bring to a clinician?</li>
</ul>

<ZenTip image="/app-ui/zen_new_low.webp">
  Read the week back in <strong>one sitting</strong>. Patterns are easier to spot all at once than day by day.
</ZenTip>

<p>A short personal log can't diagnose a disorder or tell coincidence from cause.</p>
<p>Symptoms that keep going deserve care, whatever any score says.</p>
<p>Continue with the <a href="/stress/apple-watch/">Apple Watch guide</a>, <a href="/how-it-works/">Cortisol+ methodology</a> or <a href="/tools/">free check-ins</a>.</p>
<script>
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    document.getElementById('print-journal')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
  });
</script>
<style>
  @media print {
    :global(header#site-nav), :global(footer), :global(aside), :global(nav), :global(.reading-progress), :global([data-start-cta]) { display: none !important; }
    :global(article) { padding: 0 !important; max-width: none !important; }
    .journal-day { break-inside: avoid; }
    textarea { min-height: 4em; }
  }
</style>
</ArticleLayout>
